---
// What reaches the model when it replies.
---

<figure class="diagram" aria-label="What the model sees when it replies">
  <div class="diagram-row">
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>Every request</strong>
      <p>
        The memory section: profiles of the people it works with and the
        roster. Changes only when a profile or the roster does, so the
        provider's prompt cache holds.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>Every message</strong>
      <p>
        Automatic recall: a search on the message's own words. Up to 20 items,
        oldest first, appended after the message for that reply only.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="diagram-box">
      <strong>When it decides</strong>
      <p>
        <code>recall</code> searches everything, optionally between two dates.
        <code>read_memory</code> opens a page, a note or a whole exchange.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="diagram-arrow">all evidence carries its date, who said it and where</div>
  <div class="diagram-box accent">
    <strong>The reply</strong>
    <p>
      Written by the chat model, which sees the recent conversation verbatim
      and everything else through memory.
    </p>
  </div>
</figure>
